*> The baby axolotl keyframe animations (docs/protocol/34-entity-models-8-aquatic-nautilus-boats.md 4.4, 4.5, Appendix A.1; 34-1 5.2, 5.3, 5.5): the seven animations are rows of the keyframe
*> data (EM3-ANIM-DEF ordinals 12 to 18: swim, walk floor, walk floor underwater, idle underwater, idle floor underwater, idle floor, play dead), EF8-BABY-AXOLOTL-ANIM applies them as the render
*> state's animation states say (the walk floor and its underwater companion both for the walk state, as the document reads it) and the replica chooses the state (ENTITY-AXOLOTL-TICK).
*> The expected offsets come from an independent evaluator of the document's tables (scratchpad/models/baby_axolotl.py); a few keyframes are also typed from the document by hand.
